idlands and the north to grow it also  helps to relieve the pressure on uh  green fields that is good for the  environment as I say you're a very busy  man I heard you in the House of Commons  earlier in the week um saying that you  feel sorry for younger people than you  do potentially for pensioners that's not  going to go down very well with the  Bedrock of conservative supporters does  it um well my mum and dad are pensioners  and I'm naturally on their side but one  of the points that I was making is we  have to recognize that over the course  of in the last few years for a variety  of reasons partly the rest of you have  covered young people are having a a  challenging time and I want to make sure  that we extend opportunity to the Next  Generation and that means both building  the homes that they need but also making  sure that we get our economy onto an  even Keel um after the the turbulence of  covid and the war in Ukraine and provide  them with the opportunities that they  need in order to succeed in the future  talk to me about Michelle moan what do  you remember about the PPE contract with  Michelle moon when she approached you  how did that conversation go well during  the pandemic there were lots of people  who were approaching us with offers of  PPE I referred all of them to the  appropriate Civil Service channels in  order to make sure that the uh PPE that  we were being offered was of sufficient  quality and could be sourced in time it  was a procurement process which every  offer went through in order to assess  she did approach you with your personal  email no well lots of people approach to  be um  yeah there were lots of people who  approached me whether it was through  email text  um or uh or uh uh in the precincts of  the House of Commons or wherever to uh  uh say that they could help us because  as you'll remember at the time  um not just in the United Kingdom  um but across Europe uh we needed to  Source PPE quickly  um and uh anyone who approached me I  said thank you very much and made sure  that uh their uh their efforts to help  were referred to the appropriate  officially run independent channel to  assess whether or not the PPE that they  were offering um was value for money so  what do you remember about the personal  email that she sent you  um uh that she was one of uh a huge  number of people who were approaching  the government at the time uh who were  so you don't remember specifically her  approaching you uh I remember lots of  people approaching me you remember her  specifically approaching you I do  remember the thing about um baroness  moon is that uh uh uh you know as you  know she's a strong personality  um but there were lots and lots of other  people who approached me as well anyone  who approached me I thanked and then  made sure that they went through the  appropriate process so that anyone's  claim was assessed not by me as an  individual but by an independent process  okay but what do you remember about her  personal approach to you what do you  remember about that email uh that I  remember that she was uh Keen to ensure  that uh PPE which the government needed  at that time was provided  so you can't remember exactly what she  said uh well lots of people approached  me at the time I'm asking about her  specifically yeah I know and I'm saying  that lots of people approached me so uh  uh what I can recall is that she said  that the uh there was an organization  that she believed would be able to  provide PPE for the government and I  said to her as I said to everyone thank  you very much that's very kind we do  need PPE but I'm not the person who can  make that decision as to whether or not  this contract should be awarded okay but  you did forward on that uh that contact  and yeah as I did with lots of people  because  specifically about her how do you feel  about the fact that millions of pounds  was wasted because of that introduction  well uh I don't know uh uh the detail of 