ified if it had been me  um uh because because there's a lot of  money that's been wasted yes of course  it is and of course the one of the  things is that none of us want that  money to be wasted but the the uh the  problems that we had with PPE at the  time meant that we were anxious to scale  contracts from everyone the fact that  some contracts meant that some of the  material that was uh procured was not  upstairs a decision that was made in  haste  um well everyone was making that  decision it's correct everyone's making  that decision on the basis of what  individual organizations put forward and  what the independent process decided I  did not decide  to award that contract  you didn't you're right I'm talking  about energy  are you having my water yes  I wonder how you're saving energy at  home because the Chancellor's telling us  that we need to save 15 on our energy  bills what are you going to do uh well  at home I try to you as much as possible  make sure that uh I turn down the  thermostat uh that I uh limit my energy  use but again I'm conscious that uh as a  minister I'm in a relatively comfortable  position compared to uh to to many  others so I think the right thing to do  is to make sure that we Safeguard people  with the energy price guarantee and we  also provide people with routes to get  the advice that they want on how to  minimize their energy usage we know that  you're a very healthy man we often see  you out running  um when you do need to go to the doctor  do you use a private GP uh I uh wherever  possible always use the NHS but I have  on occasion used private medicine  um we know that the Prime Minister does  that as well is that what do you think  that says about the optics for people  when they have to wait a fortnight for  their GP and the boss who is in charge  of of that system can spend 250 quid and  just I think the most important thing is  making sure that all of us do what we  can in order to ensure that the NHS gets  the resources that it needs  so you support him using a private GP  when he wants to uh I think everybody  that's got enough money should use a  private GP to take pressure off the  system uh no I wouldn't give anyone else  any advice about their own Healthcare  choices  I have a question before I let you go  these pesky 100 ml bottles at the  airports apparently that's going to be  scrapped with these new scanners I don't  know if you've heard that or not  um how relieved are you about that  um well whenever I fly I always take a  minimum level of cosmetic and other  ambulance uh uh with me so I don't think  it will make much of a difference to me  but for those people whom it will make  flying more convenient I'm delighted  it's great to see you um take the water  with you we'll make your question thank  you very much indeed as always great

